HEK MTRF1/MTRF1A double KO processing notes
1. How to use this document
README.md explains the numbered Python/R workflow. This document records the original processing commands and alternative analyses, with headings for steps and historical samples.
Step	Tool / output
Trim adapters and filter lengths	Cutadapt → trimmed FASTQ
Align to the selected reference	Bowtie2 → alignment files
Filter, sort and index mapped reads	SAMtools → sorted, indexed BAM
Review offsets and read phasing	plastid psite / phase_by_size
Export counts and nucleotide vectors	plastid counts_in_region / get_count_vectors
Analyze occupancy and make plots	02_analyze_vectors.R; see README.md

Select an analysis branch and check its inputs, reference coordinates, length filters and offsets before reuse. Historical tool spelling, filenames and sample IDs are retained.
